-- title:
--   A U_ℓ-step lattice never contains the level lattice
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ be nonzero and work in the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and every order containing it equals it. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $m$ a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ such that $m$ and $N\cdot m^{-1}$ both lie in [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every height-one prime; assume further that `meetOrder` $\Lambda_1\,m=\Lambda_1\sqcap$ `conjByFiniteIdele` $\Lambda_1\,m$ has relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive subgroups. Let $\ell$ be a prime dividing $N$ and let $h$ be an adelic unit in `levelHeckeUSet` $\Lambda_1\,R\,\ell$ for $R=$ `meetOrder` $\Lambda_1\,m$: that is, $h$ and $\ell\cdot h^{-1}$ lie in the adelic box of $R$ while $h^{-1}$ and $\ell^{-1}h$ do not, the conjugate `conjByFiniteIdele` $R\,h$ differs from $R$, and $R\not\le$ `conjByFiniteIdele` $\Lambda_1\,h$. Then for every adelic unit $x$ the lattice [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda_1\,(xm)$, namely the set of $z$ in the algebra with $z\otimes 1\in (xm)\cdot$ `finiteAdeleBox` $\Lambda_1$, is not contained in [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda_1\,(xh)$.
--
--   This is one of the local Iwahori-level statements at a prime $\ell$ dividing the level, expressing that a $U_\ell$-step from the vertex $\Lambda_1$ leaves the edge determined by $m$: the sublattice produced by $h$ never contains the lattice attached to $m$. It feeds the comparison of the $U_\ell$-Hecke count on the class set graph of the Eichler order $\Lambda_1\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$ with the corresponding count of subgroups on the elliptic-curve side.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_LevelU_not_le_of_mem_levelHeckeUSet.lean

